  "created": "2026-11-14T17:20:27.327Z",
  "description": "A source generator on top of RabbitMQ to minimize the boiler plate needed to get started. Just add a [Consumer] attribute to a function to get started!",
  "id": "MinimalRabbit",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-14T17:23:36.333Z",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "tqhN+A5Mv2h69SVg+7fqiA6FvrEU7QQMgwFUuMxYQUli+QF7fPpyadvFB8rE2f+Gk51ez17b1O+oOITXuSV6Ew==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 224545,
  "published": "2026-11-14T17:20:27.327Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking Changes\n\n- Queue declarations are now strongly typed using Queue<TMessage>.\n- Consumer registration moved from methods to partial consumer classes.\n- Publisher methods must use the generated PublishAsync contract.\n- Dependency injection is now the preferred mechanism for accessing services and RabbitMQ context within consumers.\n\nNew Features\n\n- Added fan-out support.\n- Added structural fan-out support.\n- Added parametric fan-out support.\n- Added fan-in operations.\n- Added pluggable fan-operation management via IFanOperationManager.\n\nUpgrade Notes\n\n- Update all queue declarations to specify a message type.\n- Move consumer attributes from methods to consumer classes.\n- Rename publisher methods to PublishAsync where required.\n- Verify all publishers and consumers use the queue's declared message type.",
